-2. EAS ANDROID BUILD + PLAY STORE SUBMIT (follow-up to -1 below, same day):
    - First production build attempt (792db38e, versionCode 4) ERRORED at the
      "Run gradlew" step. Root cause found by reading the full Gradle log
      (not just the top-level error summary): the @sentry/react-native
      Gradle plugin's auto source-map-upload task
      (createBundleReleaseJsAndAssets_SentryUpload) failed with
      "An organization ID or slug is required (provide with --org)" --
      Sentry was wired into the app (see -1 below) but no real org/project/
      auth token was ever configured, so the CLI upload step had nothing to
      authenticate against and failed the whole Gradle build.
    - Fix: added SENTRY_DISABLE_AUTO_UPLOAD=true to all 4 eas.json build
      profiles (development, development-client, preview, production) so
      the upload task is skipped instead of failing the build. Committed
      as 0a28642 and pushed to master.
    - Second build (015c23fb, versionCode 5) succeeded -- .aab artifact
      produced.
    - `eas submit` to the Play Store internal track initially failed:
      "The service account is missing the necessary permissions to submit
      the app to Google Play Store." Root cause (verified live in Play
      Console via browser): the eas-builder@play-console-api-499011.iam.
      gserviceaccount.com service account had never been invited as a user
      under Users and permissions -- 0 access, not just insufficient
      access. This is an account-permission change, so it was left for the
      user to grant (out of scope for automated action) rather than
      fixed directly.
    - User granted the service account Admin app-permission on P-Search via
      Play Console; verified in-browser (Users and permissions >
      eas-builder@... > Permissions for P-Search > "Admin (all
      permissions)" checked).
    - Re-ran `eas submit` on the existing build (no rebuild needed) --
      SUCCEEDED. Submission 74c189e1-96df-4c8b-a5dc-9f0e0b474f5a, app now
      live on the Play Store internal testing track as versionCode 5.
